@startuml activity_fleet_planner_modes

skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12

title Fleet Planners — Who Chooses the Routes?

start

if (--compare?) then (yes)
  :Run five variants independently:\nDistance / Independent;\nSolo / Independent;\nAdaptive / Independent;\nAdaptive / Cooperative;\nAdaptive / CBS;
  stop
else (single planner)
endif

:Select planner;\nDefault = Independent;

if (Independent?) then (yes)
  :For each train, run its own path search;
  :Other trains do not affect its initial route;
elseif (Cooperative?) then (yes)
  :Order trains by departure time,\nthen name;
  :Route each train using earlier trains'\nreservation tolls;
  :Reserve each selected route;
  :Refine the fleet routes with dry-run cost\nand expected event delay when supplied;
  note right
    RefinedPlanner compares independent
    and prioritized seeds, then tries
    one-rail alternatives (up to 3 passes).
    Keep only whole-fleet gains >= 1 s.
    Event risk is included when Adaptive
    supplies the fleet risk map.
  end note
else (CBS)
  :Create independent routes and a\nprioritized fallback solution;
  while (Conflict found and budget remains?) is (yes)
    :Choose the first overlapping,\nopposite-direction single-line conflict;
    :Branch: forbid that rail for train A\nor forbid it for train B;
    :Re-route the affected train;\nqueue branches by fleet cost;
  endwhile (no conflict / budget reached)
  :Return best conflict-free solution found,\nor the prioritized fallback;
  note right
    At most 200 expansions by default.
    Conflict branching needs --lines;
    without it there are no modeled
    head-on conflicts to resolve.
    Route-set cost adds expected event
    delay to the event-free fleet time.
  end note
endif

if (Rail event during a cooperative/CBS run?) then (yes)
  :Reconsider only trains not yet departed;
  :Switch once per train only when own gain\nis at least 30 s and no greater than\nother trains' added cost;
else (no)
endif

note right
  CLI: Cooperative/CBS default to Adaptive unless a path mode is explicit.
  --lines is an independent track-safety option, not a planner.
end note

stop

@enduml
